And now, for the real spoiler:

Eating rings can add intrinsics.  To eat a ring, you must become a monster
that can eat the ring's material.  If, in a given game, the ring of adornment
is metal of some sort, or of another material that SOME monster can eat,
then you can eat edible rings (for your current form) and have a 1 in 3 
chance of gaining that intrinsic.  This DOES work for adornment as a permanent
charisma gain, but it's not easy to get lots of rings of adornment, sometimes.

Furthermore, using a blessed charging effect (from the PYEC or a scroll)
to charge a ring with plusses (adornment, increase damage, increase strength,
protection, and such), then the bonus will increase.  There's a distressing
tendency for the charged ring to evaporate after +2, though, so do watch it.

hope this all helps, and don't be eating those rings of conflict, unless
you're sure you can Hack it ;)

